  "question": {
    "text": "If the function\n$f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}\\frac{2}{x}\\left\\{\\sin \\left(k_1+1\\right) x+\\sin \\left(k_2-1\\right) x\\right\\}, \\quad x \\lt 0 \\\\ 4, \\quad x=0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} \\log _e\\left(\\frac{2+k_1 x}{2+k_2 x}\\right), \\quad x\\gt0\\end{array}\\right.$\nis continuous at $\\mathrm{x}=0$, then $\\mathrm{k}_1^2+\\mathrm{k}_2^2$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "kUcKl",
      "text": "$20$",
